+---
+title: 'v2 ambience bed — the Suno music loop in the game'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-08-23'
+status: 'in-review'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+baseline_commit: '339e173'
+context:
+  - '{project-root}/assets/audio/README.md'
+  - '{project-root}/app/audio/audio.odin'
+---
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The user's Suno ambient track ("Warm Analog Drift", the flow-state
+bed candidate, fun-test verdict IN) never plays in-game — the game has only
+#81's event SFX (stings/clicks/chimes), no music bed.
+
+**Approach:** Ship a compressed seamless loop of the track as a raylib-streamed
+music bed, layered BESIDE the #81 event system (never into it): a new
+`assets/audio/ambience_loop.ogg` slot + bed playback/ducking/level logic in
+`app/audio/audio.odin`, driven per-frame from `app/main.odin`. Presentation-only:
+the sim, T1/T2 goldens and replay hashes cannot move.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Audio stays presentation-only: no Run_State writes, no sim-rng draws, no
+  new cosmetic-rng draws (the #81 consumer's draw pattern is T1-pinned —
+  the bed adds ZERO draws).
+- No audio-device failure may crash headless/CI: the bed loads and plays ONLY
+  when `device_on` (the #81 silent-fallback precedent); a missing/undecodable
+  OGG silently means "no bed".
+- Respect #81's event system: layer beside it (append-only event tags remain
+  the SFX path; `consumer_consume`/`Pending`/`audio_flush` unchanged in shape).
+- Mute (M key + settings row) must mute the bed too; captions stay live.
+- The 35MB vault WAV is never committed — only the ~0.9MB OGG + a documented,
+  reproducible transform script.
+- Loop points, ducking approach, and asset sizes must land in the PR body.
+
+**Ask First:**
+- None known — the briefing delegates loop length (~2min), ducking style, and
+  pause behavior to the minion ("minion's call", "minion picks, document").
+
+**Never:**
+- No golden re-bless, no .dem/.log.bin edits, no sim/catalog changes.
+- No sidechain/audio-graph machinery beyond raylib's API (raylib has no
+  sidechain — the duck is an app-side volume envelope; a conservative fixed
+  level would also be acceptable but the envelope is strictly better).
+- No per-state tracks / intensity layers (the vault README's mood plan is a
+  stage-3 candidate — record it, don't build it).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| HAPPY_PATH | device on, OGG present | bed plays from boot, loops seamlessly (125.6s), events duck it | n/a |
+| NO_DEVICE (headless/CI) | `IsAudioDeviceReady()` false | no bed, no crash — SFX/captions unchanged | `bed_on = false`, all bed procs early-return |
+| MISSING_OGG | file absent or frameCount 0 | game runs exactly as before (SFX + placeholders only) | silent skip, stderr note |
+| PAUSED (5.3) | mode Paused | bed keeps playing at `MUSIC_VOLUME × MUSIC_PAUSE_LEVEL` (soft-lower, NOT a cut) | n/a |
+| GAME_OVER | mode Game_Over | bed keeps playing at full bed level (calm) | n/a |
+| MUTE | M key / settings row | bed pauses in place (resume continues where it left off) | n/a |
+| EVENT_BURST | flush stages ≥1 play | duck envelope: deep duck `MUSIC_DUCK_SECS`, then ramp back over `MUSIC_DUCK_RAMP_SECS` | n/a |
+
