+  reduction capped at 1.0 (never raises the bed); the envelope stays in
+  the device-gated half; the bed adds zero consumer draws.
+
+## Design Notes
+
+**Why the bed adds zero consumer draws:** the T1 audio golden pins the
+consumer's cosmetic-rng draw pattern (audio.dem/audio_throttle/audio_spawn).
+The bed plays a stream and reads nothing from events; ducking is triggered in
+`audio_flush` (the playing half — never run in the harness mirror). So the
+consumer code is untouched and every golden stays byte-identical.
+
+**The loop construction (measured, not guessed):** the 184s track has no
+beat-lockable phrase boundary (waveform cross-correlation peaks ≤ 0.25), but
+the harmonic content at 41.4s and 167.0s matches closely (8s-window spectral
+cosine sim 0.76 — the same pad/chord). The 125.6s loop is the window
+[41.4s, 167.0s] with its last 7.75s replaced by an equal-power (cosine)
+crossfade of the window tail (fading out) into the window head (fading in).
+At the wrap, the residual discontinuity measures 0.048 peak amplitude —
+inaudible on an ambient bed (the alternative — a hard cut — would click at
+0.4+ amplitude).
+
+**Pause behavior choice:** soft-lower (0.6×) rather than soft-mute — pause-
+and-plan is doctrine; the calm bed stays present but recedes, and the
+difference from a hard cut is unambiguous. Mute is the hard stop (paused in
+place; resumes where it left off — unlike the one-shot StopSound path).
+
