+## What
+
+The user's Suno ambient bed now plays in-game (the 2026-08-23 report: "i dont hear the ambient song"). One calm, seamless music loop layered **beside** the #81 event-sound system — never into it.
+
+## Loop points (data, not guesses)
+
+- **Window:** [41.4 s, 167.0 s] of the vault source — **125.6 s** (the two regions with the highest harmonic similarity in the track: 8 s-window spectral cosine similarity **0.76**).
+- **Crossfade:** the last **7.75 s** of the loop are an equal-power (cosine) crossfade of the window tail into the window head (blend-at-end). The track has **no beat-lockable phrase boundary** (waveform cross-correlation peaks ≤ 0.25), so a hard cut would click (0.4+ amplitude); the crossfade construction measures **0.048 peak** residual discontinuity at the wrap (printed by the build script).
+- **Reproducible:** `tools/build_ambience_loop.py` rebuilds the committed OGG byte-identically (sha256-pinned).
+
+## Ducking approach
+
+raylib has **no sidechain support**, so the duck is an **app-side volume envelope**: any played event sound (wire click, spawn chime, crisis sting, arrival tick) ducks the bed to `MUSIC_DUCK_VOLUME/MUSIC_VOLUME` (0.12 at the default master 0.40) for `MUSIC_DUCK_SECS` (0.30 s), then ramps back over `MUSIC_DUCK_RAMP_SECS` (0.60 s). The duck is a **relative reduction capped at 1.0** — it never raises the bed. #81's sounds stay clearly audible.
+
+## Asset sizes
+
+| Asset | Size | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| `assets/audio/ambience_loop.ogg` | **913,706 bytes (0.91 MB)** — vorbis 48 kHz stereo, 125.6 s | committed; sha256 `7fdb30925eba3f8490895742a69ffebba16643d2ebd4f5dfe5cf88329a06d609` |
+| vault `Warm Analog Drift.wav` | 35,359,760 bytes (35 MB) — PCM s16le 48 kHz stereo | **never committed**; transform documented in `assets/audio/README.md` |
+
+## Determinism & headless
+
+- **T1/T2/replay byte-identical:** 48/48 demos green, zero golden diffs — the bed adds **zero** consumer draws (the T1 audio golden pins the cosmetic-rng draw pattern; the harness mirror never calls `bed_update`).
+- **Headless/CI-safe:** bed load + play gate on `IsAudioDeviceReady()` (the #81 silent-fallback precedent); a missing/undecodable OGG prints one stderr note and the game plays exactly as before.
+- All 11 local CI gates green (`tools/ci-local.sh --mac`).
+
+## Placement decisions (briefing-delegated, documented in `assets/audio/README.md`)
+
+- **Pause (5.3):** keep playing **low** (`MUSIC_PAUSE_LEVEL` 0.6×) — soft-lower, never a hard cut; the bed resumes calmly. Mute is the hard stop (pauses in place; the duck envelope resets so unmute lands at the normal level).
+- **Boot:** no title screen exists (Boot collapses into Run) — the bed starts with the run, with a ~0.6 s fade-in (the recovery ramp reused).
+- **Volume knob:** `MUSIC_VOLUME` is the named master tunable (plus `MUSIC_DUCK_VOLUME`/`MUSIC_DUCK_SECS`/`MUSIC_DUCK_RAMP_SECS`/`MUSIC_PAUSE_LEVEL`); the existing M-key + settings-row mute also mutes the bed.
+- **Stage-3 candidate (recorded, not built):** the vault README's mood plan (intensity layers → flow/tension/crisis via existing state hooks) is noted in `assets/audio/README.md`.
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **OGG not WAV in-repo:** 0.91 MB vs 35 MB; raylib streams OGG via stb_vorbis; the WAV source stays vaulted (transform script + sha256 make the provenance auditable). The 24 MB encode intermediate is gitignored.
+- **Relative duck over an absolute floor:** an absolute floor would raise the bed when the user tunes the master below it; the capped relative reduction keeps ducking monotone and the docs honest (r1 review fold).
+- **Review-swarm r1 folds (3 hunters, 3 panes):** duck cap, mute envelope reset + `bed_paused` mirror flag (headless-testable mute branch), `StopMusicStream` before unload, boot fade-in, `pending_any_plays` single-source family list, `bed_envelope_step` bed_on gate, build-script guards + timeout + sha256. All folded; 17 audio unit tests now cover the pure envelope/level/mute state machine.
+- **Canon note (known bmad tooling HALT):** `bmad-quick-dev` → `bmad-build` render HALTs on this install (`ambiguous config value implementation_artifacts` — bmm + gds both define it; upstream 6.11.0, Silas-waived). Workflow step files were followed directly; the waiver is carried per the night-watchman field note.
+- **No CI-gate change for the OGG:** a broken asset surfaces at runtime with a clear stderr note; the committed sha256 lets any reviewer cross-check the binary (a decode gate would require touching the GH workflow + its local replica — deferred).
+
+## Verification
+
+- `tools/harness.sh run` → 48 demos green (T1/T2/replay byte-identical).
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` → all 11 gates green.
+- `odin test app/audio` → 17/17 (13 pre-existing + 4 new bed tests).
+- Smoke run: `AUDIO: Device initialized successfully`, `[assets/audio/ambience_loop.ogg] Music file loaded successfully`, no crash.
