+
+**The seamless loop (numbers are data):** the loop is the source window
+[41.4 s, 167.0 s] (125.6 s — the two regions with the highest harmonic
+similarity in the track, 8 s-window spectral cosine similarity 0.76), with
+its last 7.75 s replaced by an equal-power (cosine) crossfade of the window
+tail (fading out) into the window head (fading in). At the wrap the file
+returns to its own head at full level; the residual discontinuity measures
+0.048 peak amplitude (measured by the build script) — inaudible on an
+ambient bed. A hard cut would click (0.4+ amplitude — the track has no
+beat-lockable phrase boundary).
+
+**Ducking:** raylib has no sidechain support, so the duck is an app-side
+volume envelope (`app/audio/audio.odin`): any played event sound (wire
+click, spawn chime, crisis sting, arrival tick) ducks the bed to ~30% of
+its normal level (`MUSIC_DUCK_VOLUME`/`MUSIC_VOLUME` — 0.12 at the default
+master) for `MUSIC_DUCK_SECS` (0.30 s), then ramps back over
+`MUSIC_DUCK_RAMP_SECS` (0.60 s). The duck is a RELATIVE reduction, capped
+so it never raises the bed (a master tuned at or below the duck level just
+stays there — the events already sit above it). The #81 event sounds stay
+clearly audible over the bed.
+
+**Levels & modes:** `MUSIC_VOLUME` (0.40) is the named master music-volume
+tunable — the user tunes by ear. The bed starts with a short fade-in (the
+duck ramp reused — it swells from the duck level over ~0.6 s); Pause (5.3)
+soft-lowers it to `MUSIC_VOLUME × MUSIC_PAUSE_LEVEL` (keep-playing-low,
+never a hard cut; the duck stacks multiplicatively on top); Game_Over
+keeps it calm; Mute pauses it in place — instantly, deliberately (a mute
+toggle must be immediate; the bed resumes where it left off, envelope
+reset, at the normal level). The bed starts with the run (Boot collapses
+into Run — there is no title screen) and is session-level: it survives run
+restarts; only Mute stops it.
